---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
    title="tcplot | Claire Nyquist"
    description="tcplot — a meetup group for data visualization enthusiasts exploring creative and scientific plotting."
    image="/images/tcplot(whale).webp"
>
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8">
        <!-- Header -->
        <div class="text-center mb-12">
            <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl name-gradient mb-6">
                <span class="font-silkscreen font-normal">tcplot</span>
            </h1>
            <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-relaxed mb-4">
                <span class="font-silkscreen">tcplot</span> is a Twin Cities community for data visualization
                practitioners, enthusiasts, and storytellers. Whether you are a
                D3 wizard, a Tableau pro, a ggplot2 devotee, or someone who
                appreciates a well-crafted chart, you've found your people.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Colors Image -->
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-12">
            <div class="max-w-2xl w-full rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
                <img
                    src="/images/tcplot(colorswithtext).webp"
                    alt="tcplot data visualization twin cities — colorful mosaic collage of rectangular chart elements"
                    class="w-full h-auto object-contain"
                />
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- About Section -->
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-12">
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                Our mission is to elevate the data literacy and design standards
                of the MSP area through three core pillars:
            </p>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-600 mb-6">
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">▸</span>
                    <span
                        ><strong class="text-gray-900">Talks:</strong> Hear from local
                        experts and industry leaders on the "why" and "how" of great
                        visualization.</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">▸</span>
                    <span
                        ><strong class="text-gray-900">Workshops:</strong> Roll up
                        your sleeves for hands-on sessions where we master new tools,
                        libraries, and design principles.</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">▸</span>
                    <span
                        ><strong class="text-gray-900">Build-a-thons:</strong> Join
                        collaborative coworking where we take datasets and turn them
                        into impactful, interactive, or artistic visual stories.</span
                    >
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Links -->
        <div class="flex justify-center gap-6 mt-12">
            <a
                href="https://tcplot.com"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium"
            >
                tcplot.com
            </a>
            <a
                href="https://www.instagram.com/tcplot/"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium"
            >
                Instagram
            </a>
            <a
                href="https://www.meetup.com/tcplot/?eventOrigin=home_groups_you_organize"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium"
            >
                Meetup
            </a>
        </div>

        <!-- Event: Mapathon -->
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-16 mb-12">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">
                Upcoming: Mapathon — All About Maps
            </h2>

            <div class="mb-6 text-gray-700">
                <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    Saturday, October 24th · 10:00 AM to 12:00 PM CDT
                </p>
                <p class="mt-1">The Coffee Shop NE, 2852 Johnson St NE, Minneapolis, MN</p>
            </div>

            <figure class="mb-6 max-w-md">
                <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
                    <img
                        src="/images/tcplot-meiji-japan-map.webp"
                        alt="A Meiji-era outline map of Japan with prefectures hand-tinted in soft green, orange, yellow, and purple"
                        class="w-full h-auto object-contain"
                        loading="lazy"
                    />
                </div>
                <figcaption class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mt-2">
                    A Meiji-era outline map of Japan (1870s), its newly drawn prefectures hand-tinted in watercolor; public domain.
                </figcaption>
            </figure>

            <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4 italic">
                Every map is a chart with a place in it.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                A morning devoted entirely to maps, in two acts: bring one map you love (or love to hate) for a two-minute show-and-tell, then we'll build maps of our own and present them. No GIS experience needed.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                Details at <a href="https://tcplot.com/mapathon" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">tcplot.com/mapathon</a>.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Event: Opposing Data Stories -->
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-16 mb-12">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">
                Upcoming: Opposing Data Stories
            </h2>

            <div class="mb-6 text-gray-700">
                <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    Saturday, November 21st · 10:00 AM to 12:00 PM CST
                </p>
                <p class="mt-1">The Coffee Shop NE, 2852 Johnson St NE, Minneapolis, MN</p>
            </div>

            <figure class="mb-6 max-w-2xl">
                <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
                    <img
                        src="/images/tcplot-nightingale-1858.webp"
                        alt="Florence Nightingale's two rose diagrams of army deaths, dominated by blue wedges of preventable disease"
                        class="w-full h-auto object-contain"
                        loading="lazy"
                    />
                </div>
                <figcaption class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mt-2">
                    Florence Nightingale, <em>Diagram of the Causes of Mortality in the Army in the East</em> (1858); public domain.
                </figcaption>
            </figure>

            <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4 italic">
                Same data. Opposite stories.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                Solo or in pairs, we'll chart one dataset two ways, once as a crisis and once as nothing to see, without changing a single number. Then the room guesses which design choice is doing the work.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                Details at <a href="https://tcplot.com/opposing-data-stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">tcplot.com/opposing-data-stories</a>.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Event: Climate Data -->
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-16 mb-12">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">
                Upcoming: Climate Data
            </h2>

            <div class="mb-6 text-gray-700">
                <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    Saturday, December 12th · 10:00 AM to 12:00 PM CST
                </p>
                <p class="mt-1">The Coffee Shop NE, 2852 Johnson St NE, Minneapolis, MN</p>
            </div>

            <figure class="mb-6 max-w-2xl">
                <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
                    <img
                        src="/images/tcplot-msp-warming-stripes.webp"
                        alt="Warming stripes for Minneapolis and St. Paul, 1939 to 2025: vertical bands of blue and red, growing redder toward the right"
                        class="w-full h-40 sm:h-56 object-cover"
                        loading="lazy"
                    />
                </div>
                <figcaption class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mt-2">
                    Annual average temperature in Minneapolis and St. Paul, 1939 to 2025, one stripe per year in the style of Ed Hawkins&#39;s warming stripes; data from NOAA.
                </figcaption>
            </figure>

            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                Come explore the climate data provided or of your choice.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                Details at <a href="https://tcplot.com/climate" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">tcplot.com/climate</a>.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Event: Charts & Color -->
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-16 mb-12">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">
                Upcoming: Charts & Color
            </h2>

            <div class="mb-6 text-gray-700">
                <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    Saturday, January 16th · 10:00 AM to 12:00 PM CST
                </p>
                <p class="mt-1">The Coffee Shop NE, 2852 Johnson St NE, Minneapolis, MN</p>
            </div>

            <figure class="mb-6 max-w-2xl">
                <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden aspect-[3/2] bg-white">
                    <img
                        src="/images/tcplot-blood-test-reference-ranges.webp"
                        alt="A long chart of reference ranges for blood tests: dozens of overlapping colored bars on a log scale"
                        class="w-full h-full object-cover pan-chart"
                        loading="lazy"
                    />
                </div>
                <figcaption class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mt-2">
                    Mikael Häggström, <em>Reference ranges for blood tests</em> (2009); public domain (CC0).
                </figcaption>
            </figure>

            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                A morning about color in charts, in two acts: bring a chart whose color you have opinions about, then we'll recolor charts together and show the before and after.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                Details at <a href="https://tcplot.com/charts-and-color" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">tcplot.com/charts-and-color</a>.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Petri Image -->
        <div class="flex justify-center mt-12">
            <div class="max-w-2xl w-full rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
                <img
                    src="/images/tcplot(petriwithtext).webp"
                    alt="tcplot data visualization twin cities — collage featuring a scientist with a petri dish, eclipse, and time series chart"
                    class="w-full h-auto object-contain"
                />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
    .pan-chart {
        animation: pan-chart 32s ease-in-out infinite alternate;
    }
    @keyframes pan-chart {
        from {
            object-position: 0% 50%;
        }
        to {
            object-position: 100% 50%;
        }
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .pan-chart {
            animation: none;
        }
    }
</style>
